# Production build config.
#
# In dev, VITE_API_BASE_URL is the relative path "/api" — Vite's dev
# server (see vite.config.js's server.proxy) forwards it to the local
# backend, so frontend and backend never need to agree on an absolute
# origin while developing.
#
# There is no such proxy in a production static build (Cloudflare Pages,
# Netlify, etc. just serve the built files — nothing forwards /api
# anywhere). VITE_API_BASE_URL must be the real backend's absolute URL,
# baked in at build time.
#
# Recommended: set this as a build-time environment variable in your
# hosting platform's dashboard (e.g. Cloudflare Pages → Settings →
# Environment variables) rather than committing a real value here — it's
# not a secret (it ends up in the shipped JS bundle either way), but the
# real domain isn't known until you've actually provisioned the backend.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com/api
